A||||5||mshill||87GT w/T-tops $1400, good deal?||||1||
Z||000000||mshill||07-31-2000||10:56 PM||||I went to see the 87GT with T-tops this evening.  The car is maroon with 106K miles and looks great from a distance, but up close it definitely needs some work.  He was working on the top end of the engine cause some lifters wouldn't pump up leaving the front valves quite dry. I told him I wouldn't buy it until he got it running (I just don't want to have to rent a dolly to tow it home).  <P>Here's a few things that I noticed:<P>1) No drivers side sail panel.<BR>2) Cracked passenger side sail panel.<BR>3) Cracked drivers side rear tail light lense.<BR>4) Both dew wipes need to be replaced.<BR>5) Felt seal around T-tops was in bad shape.<BR>6) He said passenger side leaked a little.<BR>7) Headliner shot.<BR>8) Leather seats were pretty shoddy.<BR>9) Top plastic moulding at A and B pillars is pretty shot.<P>Some of the good stuff:<BR>1) Honeycomb wheels and rubber in good shape.<BR>2) EGR Tube intact.<BR>3) 5 speed Getrag.<BR>4) T-Tops are ingood shape.<BR>5) Stock radio/equalizer and sub-woofer intact.<BR>6) New brakes.<BR>7) Clutch hydrolics in good shape.<BR>8) Paint and trim in decent shape.<P>I told him that I would give hime $1400 cash if he could drive it to my house.  He was asking $1600 but it is obvious that he was <BR>going to settle for less.<P>Sound like a good deal?  How much to replace the T-top parts (felt and seals)?<P>Mark S.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||08-01-2000||12:25 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fieroparts.com/ttop.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroparts.com/ttop.html</A> <P>This is supposedly the last of the replacement T-top parts. <P>Take a deep breath...<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 08-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||08-01-2000||02:35 AM||||The felt seals for the T-Tops is also available from.....shhh I don't want to say it too loud......But (Ford) sells them for the (Mustangs)..It is the same parts that CC used on the Fiero T-Top kits.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 08-01-2000).]||||reg||2
Z||000003||mshill||08-01-2000||12:36 PM||||So, what do you guys do to replace the rubber seals if they are not available anymore?<P>Has anyone considered something like a hybrid seal, combining say normal Fiero door seals with a piece from a F-Bird or Camaro T-top.<P>Are there any solutions out there?||||reg||9
Z||000004||pollock||08-01-2000||01:06 PM||||sorry.....<p>[This message has been edited by pollock (edited 08-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||pollock||08-01-2000||01:10 PM||||I think you could come up with something if you needed to.  Probably wouldn't be too hard to get it to seal; the challenge would be to make it look good.  <P>Fiero Parts& Appraisals has the plastic pillar caps for about $28 each.  the "felt" P-seals are like 40 each, i think.<P>Places to look for substitutes:<BR>1.  other cars (mustangs, daytonas, f-bodies, maybe some of the import t-top cars)<BR>2.  trim shops or body shop suppliers (lots of available rubber, sold by the foot and identified by cross-section)<BR>3.  JCWhitney has rubber sold the same way.<BR>4.  industrial catalogs <BR>5.  I think TOM on this board is making some repop corner trim as well<P>I haven't explored these in any depth, but i will certainly post here if i find something good.||||reg||1
